WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.990
- Scarlett Johansson is suing Disney

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.270
over the release of the
movie "Black Widow."

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.790
ScarJo claims that she was entitled

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.150
to a percentage of the
box office receipts.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.160
But here's the thing:

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.360
Disney released the movie "Black Widow"

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.080
on their streaming platform, Disney Plus,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.230
at the same time that they
released the movie in theaters.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.410
The movie made $60 million
on the streaming service,

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.520
but only $20 million in theaters.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.667
Johansson is claiming that
the term in the contract,

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:25.190
"Theatrical release," means an
exclusive theatrical release,

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.740
meaning only in theaters for
a specific period of time

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.050
and not simultaneously
on any other platform.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.350
Disney, I'm sure, is going
to claim that, in fact,

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:33.680
the term theatrical release means

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.110
that they just have to
release the movie in theaters,

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.660
and that, so long as they do
so, they can also release it

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.190
on their streaming
platform at the same time

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.630
and they have upheld the contract.

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:43.440
We don't have the specific
contract in front of us,

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.820
but it's pretty suspicious
that the plaintiff, Johansson,

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.220
has not included that language,

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.620
or at least is only referring
to the term theatrical release

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.300
without any kind of exclusivity
clause attached to it.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.820
So, she may have a very uphill battle

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.210
in this particular lawsuit,

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.153
but we will see them in court.

